# Using Codex in {{PROJECT_NAME}}

This optional guide accompanies core/full. The default minimal output needs no
project skills or routing JSON.

## What is available

- Root `AGENTS.md` is the project instruction entrypoint.
- An installed `.agents/ai/project-map.json` supports unfamiliar-work discovery;
  it is read on demand, not automatically loaded.
- Repository skills under `.agents/skills` are discoverable by name and description.
- A full `SKILL.md` loads when explicitly invoked or when its description matches the task.
- Other docs are read on demand through `AGENTS.md`; they are not all loaded for every task.

## Daily workflow

```text
Describe the task in conversation or provide a completed task input
                ↓
Follow the classification and authorization in docs/CODEX_WORKFLOW.md
                ↓
Use a matching project skill or execute the scoped task
                ↓
Run relevant checks from docs/VERIFICATION.md
                ↓
Review the relevant diff
```

Task templates are operator-authored input, not task history. Persistent task
records are created only when explicitly requested.

### Feature

```text
Implement this feature using docs/CODEX_WORKFLOW.md. Use $context-discovery
when affected files or consumers are not already known, and apply the relevant
profile from docs/CODING_STANDARDS.md to changed source files.
```

### Verification

```text
Use $build-and-test. Verify the current diff and report every command as
pass, fail, or not run, including remaining risk.
```

### Review

```text
Use $code-review. Review the current diff and report findings first.
Do not modify files.
```

### Repeated corrections and workflow choices

```text
Review recurring evidence under docs/CODEX_WORKFLOW.md and use
conversation to present any qualifying rule candidate. Record it only after
confirmation; docs/CODING_RULES_LOG.md is an optional recording structure.
```

## Project-specific commands

See `docs/VERIFICATION.md`. Model choice is manual; project docs and skills do
not switch the active model. File/byte budgets are deterministic proxies, not
claims about actual token usage.

## What the documents cannot enforce alone

`AGENTS.md` and skills provide durable instructions, but mechanical rules should
also be enforced by the project's confirmed formatters, linters, type checks,
tests, CI, hooks, review approvals, and sandbox/command policy where available.
Adding or changing those controls requires separate task approval.
